*.pyc

# Tool suite: commit source, ignore build artifacts and generated data
tools/pigg-wrangler-dist/build/
tools/pigg-wrangler-dist/dist/
tools/bin-crawler/exported_powers/
tools/bin-crawler/**/static/cache/

# Playwright MCP test artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# Engine artifacts (src/engine/wasm/, src/engine/wasm-node/, public/engine/) are COMMITTED,
# deliberately. They are built by `npm run build:engine` from the private rebuild repo plus a
# Rust/wasm toolchain — none of which a GitHub-hosted runner has, and the rebuild being private
# means CI cannot even check it out without a secret. Committing them is what makes this repo
# self-sufficient: deploy and CI both need only Node. Refresh them with `npm run build:engine`
# and commit the result whenever the engine changes.

# Understand-Anything scratch: the tool moves superseded batch/graph JSON into a
# timestamped trash dir. 132 files of it were committed once, and it is the reason
# scripts/verify-sync.cjs scopes its wiring grep — an unscoped grep matched half of
# scripts/ inside tool scratch and was permanently red.
.ua/.trash-*/

# Debug scratch (probes, .bak snapshots, test-run logs). Individual probe
# scripts get force-added and tracked when a committed comment or doc cites
# them by path as census evidence — same convention as the canonical fork.
/.scratch/

# vitest-only flattened dataset bundles, rebuilt by globalSetup on every run
.dataset-bundles/

# Wrangler's local secrets file and its local-dev state. `.dev.vars` holds
# RESEND_API_KEY and DESKTOP_CLIENT_TOKEN when the feedback worker is run locally.
.dev.vars
.wrangler/
